docs/*
# The GitHub Pages site. `index.html` is the name Pages serves at the site
# root; the font is copied in beside it because `assets/` is above the site
# root and is ignored anyway; `.nojekyll` stops Jekyll rendering docs/README.
!docs/index.html
!docs/RobotoFlex.ttf
!docs/.nojekyll
# The page's figures. `docs/*` ignores everything by default, so an asset added
# beside index.html is invisible to Pages until it is named here — it renders
# locally from the working tree and 404s on the live site. (Figure 1 is inline
# SVG in the page itself and needs no entry.)
!docs/NanumSquareNeo-Regular.ttf
!docs/NanumSquareNeo-Bold.ttf
# The page's figures live in one folder. `docs/*` only matches direct children,
# so un-ignoring the directory is enough for git to descend into it.
!docs/figure/
!docs/reference/
docs/reference/*
!docs/reference/PR_Flim.mp4
!docs/reference/SOURCE.md

tests/
pytest.ini
scripts/*

!scripts/fetch_font.py
!scripts/fetch_streaming_model.py
!scripts/hw/
